    "image_with_text_UcUaBD": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_z74fea": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "New Solutions and Technologies",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_i8LG4i": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>With technological advancements, NADCO continues to innovate its offerings. For example, invisible ink is a fairly new option in the tamper-evident label arena and has opened up new possibilities for covert authentication.</p><p>Invisible ink technology for tamper-evident labels uses specially formulated inks that are not visible to the naked eye.</p><p>These inks are applied to labels or packaging using traditional printing methods. However, under ultraviolet (UV) light, the ink becomes visible, revealing hidden markings, messages, or codes.</p><p>The invisible markings left behind provide an additional layer of security, ensuring products remain protected without compromising aesthetics.</p>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
